<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Ui Failge</h1><p class="st-meta">450 CE – 1556 CE (approx.) · capital Daingean</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Irish midland kingdom of the O'Connor Faly, which resisted English expansion from its bogland strongholds until the plantation of Offaly in 1556.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Uí Failge, 'descendants of Failge', claimed descent from Rus Failge, a son of the legendary <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-leinster">Leinster</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cathair-mor">Cathair Mór</a>. From the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">medieval period</a> they held a kingdom in the north-west of the Kingdom of Leinster, in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-offaly">County Offaly</a>, which takes its name from them. From the 11th century their rulers were the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oconnor-faly">Ua Conchobair Failge</a>, O'Connor Faly.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their territory of bog, esker and woodland was hard for invaders to penetrate. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-norman-invasion-of-ireland">Anglo-Norman invasion</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fitzgeralds-of-kildare">FitzGeralds of Kildare</a> took their eastern lands, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oconnor-faly">O'Connors Faly</a> held the rest, raiding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-pale">Pale</a> and taking protection payments known as black rent. Their stronghold at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daingean">Daingean</a>, set among bogs, was their main fortress in the 16th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-oconnor-faly">Brian O'Connor Faly</a> rebelled and surrendered in the 1540s, the English took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daingean">Daingean</a>. In 1556 the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mary-i-of-england">Mary I</a> shired the kingdom as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-offaly">King's County</a>, with Daingean renamed Philipstown, and planted it with English settlers, ending the kingdom.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st